the United Nations Security Council is  holding an emergency meeting this  morning on Syria following the recent  suspected chemical weapons attack Russia  requested the meeting and said that top  priority should be to avert a wider war  this morning russia's Foreign Minister  claimed the attack was staged with the  help of a foreign secret service  president Trump discussed US military  options on Syria with his advisors and  American allies yesterday but has not  made a final decision David Martin is at  the Pentagon David good morning good  morning president Trump spoke with the  British prime minister last night and  the two leaders agreed that Syria's  President Assad has a history of using  chemical weapons and that something has  to be done to stop him from doing it  again I believe there was a chemical  attack and we're looking for the actual  evidence the pictures of the aftermath  of last weekend's suspected chemical  attack in Syria that killed 42 and  injured over 500 are compelling but two  critical questions remain what kind of  chemical and who was responsible CBS  News analyst Mike Morell if the  president is going to take military  action the intelligence community would  want to give him a high confidence  judgment intelligence analysts have  concluded the symptoms shown in the  videos are consistent with exposure to  chlorine gas and that some of the  victims look like they had been exposed  to a nerve agent but that's not enough  you can only really nail it down when  you get a blood sample that you have  confidence in where that blood sample  came from and what the chain of custody  was US officials say blood samples  provided by hospital workers do indeed  confirm the presence of chemicals but  they need to be sure the evidence hasn't  been doctored Assad's never been  stronger than he is today so the  opposition would want nothing more right  now than to then to significantly weaken  him with a US air strike over the past  six months US intelligence has confirmed  four other chemical attacks carried out  by the regime but none of them triggered  a military response the stakes are  higher this time because Russia has  warned the u.s. not to strike I do think  there's a possibility here of a military  confrontation between the United States  and  Russia in Syria an international team of  chemical weapons inspectors is scheduled  to arrive at the scene of the attack  tomorrow they could find soil samples  that prove what kind of chemicals were  used but that still would not answer the  question of who is responsible  gaile all right David Martin reporting  from Washington thank you
 

